.TH VISION 1
.SH NAME
vision/detect, vision/draw, vision/crop \- recognition as filters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vision/detect
[
.B -m
.I model
] [
.B -t
.I thresh
] [
.B -c
.IR class , ...
] [
.B -j
.I n
] [
.B -v
.I mnt
] [
.I file ...
]
.br
.B vision/draw
[
.B -d
.I dir
] [
.B -o
.BR bit | png
]
.br
.B vision/crop
[
.B -d
.I dir
] [
.B -o
.BR bit | png
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each is a filter over records, lines of
.IB attr = value
fields, so anything can stand between them:
.IR grep (1),
.IR awk (1),
a file, a person.
.PP
.I Detect
writes each
.I file
named, or with none each name read from standard input one a line, to a
session of
.IR visionfs (4)
at
.I mnt
(default
.BR /mnt/vision ),
and prints what was found, the file's name first, in the order the
files were named:
.IP
.EX
file=photos/a.jpg class=dog score=0.91 x0=88 y0=140 x1=402 y1=455
file=photos/b.jpg
.EE
.PP
A file in which nothing was found is a line of its name alone.
.B -m
names the model,
.B -t
the threshold,
.B -c
the classes to keep;
.B -j
runs
.I n
sessions at once.
.PP
.I Draw
reads records and draws each box (\c
.B x0 y0 x1 y1\c
) with its label (\c
.BR label= ,
or else
.B class=
and
.BR score= )
on the picture named by
.BR file= ,
a colour for each class, and writes the picture to
.I dir
(default
.BR . )
under its own name with
.B .bit
(an uncompressed
.IR image (6))
or
.B .png
added; it prints the names it writes.
It knows nothing of models: the records may have come from anywhere.
.PP
.I Crop
reads records and writes each box as a picture of its own,
.IB dir / name . n .bit
or
.BR .png ,
.I n
counting the boxes of each picture from 0, and prints the names, so a
second model can look at what a first found.
.PP
None of them needs a display.
.SH EXAMPLES
Every picture in a directory, drawn with what was found:
.EX
; ls /photos/*.jpg | vision/detect | vision/draw -d /out -o png
.EE
.PP
Only the people, kept:
.EX
; vision/detect /photos/*.jpg > found
; grep 'class=person' found | vision/draw -d /people
.EE
.PP
A second model on the first's dogs:
.EX
; vision/detect *.jpg | grep 'class=dog' | vision/crop -d /tmp/dogs | vision/detect -m breeds
.EE
.PP
Quote a pattern with
.B =
in it: the shell takes a bare
.B =
for its own.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/vision
.br
.B /appl/lib/visrec.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR visionfs (4)
